Per-PC dispatch profiling for the CoreMark runner.

Replaces the counting fetcher with one that also records, per guest PC, how many
times it was dispatched and how many times a relative branch there was taken. It
also takes the ELF from the environment rather than from the build script, so one
build can profile every configuration a sweep produced.

Not wired into the repository. Apply with `git apply`, then:

  ELF=<coremark.elf> PROFILE_OUT=run.prof COREMARK_DISPATCH_COUNT=1 \
    COREMARK_ITERATIONS=1000 cargo run --release -p ab-riscv-coremark-runner
  riscv64-unknown-elf-objdump -d <coremark.elf> > dis.txt
  python3 annotate-profile.py dis.txt run.prof

which writes run.prof.funcs (per-function dispatch totals, sorted) and
run.prof.annot (annotated disassembly, one line per instruction with its dispatch
count and taken count). That is what found everything in
`interpreter-targeted-codegen.md` §9.

